{
  "about": "The docs sections in menu order. build.mjs assembles them into the one docs page, docs.html, and generates its side nav from this file: each category is a <details> in the nav, and each section a link to #<id> (build.mjs header comment, step 3). Per section: id, the section's id (one or two lowercase hyphenated words, PLAN.md Decision 7), which its file site/docs/sections/<id>.html puts on its hgroup's h1, and which names that file in the section's edit link, written by the build; label, its nav link as HTML, only where that is not the h1's content, which the link takes otherwise; and readme, only where the section covers a part of femto's README.md: the exact text of that part's H2 or H3 heading at the vendored commit (git -C ../femto show <the commit in site/vendor/femto/SOURCE>:README.md), the heading line after its #s, trimmed, as a string, or true for the heading whose text is the section's h1. Every README H2 but Contributing and License is named by at least one section, and npm run vendor lists, for each README section that changed, the sections that name it. The build ignores readme. The migration section's readme is true, since its heading's text holds the name criterion 14 allows only in that section's own file.",
